<section class="temple-vaastu__section temple-vaastu__section--perspective"><div class="temple-vaastu__container temple-vaastu__split"><div><p class="temple-vaastu__eyebrow">01 / The perspective</p><h2 class="temple-vaastu__title">A temple is a sacred <em style="color:#c8281e">expression of cosmic order</em></h2><div class="temple-vaastu__ornament temple-vaastu__ornament--left"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 30" width="260" height="30" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="#c47f0e" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M0 15H96M164 15H260" stroke-opacity=".75"/><path d="M130 3C139 9 141 19 130 27C119 19 121 9 130 3Z"/><path d="M130 27C122 26 113 21 109 11C118 11 126 17 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C138 26 147 21 151 11C142 11 134 17 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C119 28 107 25 100 18C111 15 123 19 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C141 28 153 25 160 18C149 15 137 19 130 27Z"/></g><circle cx="90" cy="15" r="2.4" fill="#c8281e"/><circle cx="170" cy="15" r="2.4" fill="#c8281e"/><circle cx="130" cy="15" r="2.6" fill="#c8281e"/></svg></div>
<p class="temple-vaastu__text">In the Indian shastric tradition, a temple is a sacred architectural expression of the relationship between the divine, nature and human life.</p>
<p class="temple-vaastu__text">From the selection of land and the orientation of the Garbhagriha to the placement of the deity and the arrangement of Mandapas, every element contributes to the sacred purpose of the temple.</p>
<p class="temple-vaastu__text">Rooted in the traditions of Vaastu Shastra and Shilpa Shastra, temple architecture brings together sacred geometry, directional principles and the architectural and ritual requirements of the respective temple tradition.</p>
<p class="temple-vaastu__text">Dr. Ravi Rao provides specialized guidance to ensure that these principles are appropriately integrated into temple planning and development.</p>
