<section class="temple-vaastu__section temple-vaastu__section--cream temple-vaastu__section--scope" id="services"><div class="temple-vaastu__container"><div class="temple-vaastu__header temple-vaastu__header--center"><p class="temple-vaastu__eyebrow">03 / Scope of consultation</p><h2 class="temple-vaastu__title">Every element has<br class="temple-vaastu__break"> its sacred place</h2><div class="temple-vaastu__ornament"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 30" width="260" height="30" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="#c47f0e" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M0 15H96M164 15H260" stroke-opacity=".75"/><path d="M130 3C139 9 141 19 130 27C119 19 121 9 130 3Z"/><path d="M130 27C122 26 113 21 109 11C118 11 126 17 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C138 26 147 21 151 11C142 11 134 17 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C119 28 107 25 100 18C111 15 123 19 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C141 28 153 25 160 18C149 15 137 19 130 27Z"/></g><circle cx="90" cy="15" r="2.4" fill="#c8281e"/><circle cx="170" cy="15" r="2.4" fill="#c8281e"/><circle cx="130" cy="15" r="2.6" fill="#c8281e"/></svg></div><p class="temple-vaastu__text">Temple Vaastu consultation involves a comprehensive assessment of the site, architectural layout and the individual elements that serve the sacred purpose of the temple.</p></div><div class="temple-vaastu__scope-grid"><div class="temple-vaastu__scope-card"><div class="temple-vaastu__medallion"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 18h18M6.5 18a5.5 5.5 0 0 1 11 0M12 6v2.6M4.9 9.4l1.8 1.8M19.1 9.4l-1.8 1.8"/></svg></div><h3>Land Selection &amp; Site Assessment</h3><p>Assessment of the land, topography, access roads and surrounding environment.</p></div><div class="temple-vaastu__scope-card"><div class="temple-vaastu__medallion"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 21V9a7 7 0 0 1 14 0v12M9 21v-6a3 3 0 0 1 6 0v6"/></svg></div><h3>Temple Orientation &amp; Spatial Planning</h3><p>Orientation of the temple, entrances, Pradakshina Patha and the overall spatial layout of the complex.</p></div><div class="temple-vaastu__scope-card"><div class="temple-vaastu__medallion"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2.5L15 6.5H9ZM8.5 6.5L6.5 10.5H17.5L15.5 6.5M6 10.5V20.5H18V10.5M10 20.5V15.5H14V20.5"/></svg></div><h3>Garbhagriha Planning</h3><p>Location, orientation and proportions of the principal sanctum, in accordance with the relevant temple tradition.</p></div><div class="temple-vaastu__scope-card"><div class="temple-vaastu__medallion"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2.5c2.6 2.6 3.6 4.7 3.6 6.7a3.6 3.6 0 0 1-7.2 0c0-2 1-4.1 3.6-6.7zM4 14h16c0 3.6-3.4 6-8 6s-8-2.4-8-6z"/></svg></div><h3>Murti Placement</h3><p>Placement and orientation of the murti within the sanctum.</p></div><div class="temple-vaastu__scope-card"><div class="temple-vaastu__medallion"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8l9-4 9 4M5 8v11M10 8v11M14 8v11M19 8v11M3 20h18"/></svg></div><h3>Temple Layout &amp; Sacred Elements</h3><p>Planning of additional shrines, Mandapas, halls, courtyards, Yajna Shalas and other sacred elements.</p></div><div class="temple-vaastu__scope-card"><div class="temple-vaastu__medallion"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2.5l1.6 2H10.4zM9 4.5h6l1 3H8zM7.5 7.5h9l1 3.2h-11zM6 10.7h12l1 3.3H5zM4.5 14h15v6h-15zM10.5 20v-3.2h3V20"/></svg></div><h3>Vaastu Assessment &amp; Corrections</h3><p>Evaluation of existing temple structures, identification of Vaastu defects and recommendations that respect the architectural integrity and ritual traditions of the temple.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="temple-vaastu__section temple-vaastu__section--muhurta" id="muhurta"><div class="temple-vaastu__container"><div class="temple-vaastu__header temple-vaastu__header--center"><p class="temple-vaastu__eyebrow">04 / Sacred Muhurta</p><h2 class="temple-vaastu__title">The right moment for<br class="temple-vaastu__break"> every sacred beginning</h2><div class="temple-vaastu__ornament"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 30" width="260" height="30" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="#c47f0e" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M0 15H96M164 15H260" stroke-opacity=".75"/><path d="M130 3C139 9 141 19 130 27C119 19 121 9 130 3Z"/><path d="M130 27C122 26 113 21 109 11C118 11 126 17 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C138 26 147 21 151 11C142 11 134 17 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C119 28 107 25 100 18C111 15 123 19 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C141 28 153 25 160 18C149 15 137 19 130 27Z"/></g><circle cx="90" cy="15" r="2.4" fill="#c8281e"/><circle cx="170" cy="15" r="2.4" fill="#c8281e"/><circle cx="130" cy="15" r="2.6" fill="#c8281e"/></svg></div><p class="temple-vaastu__text">In temple building, timing is part of the sacred work. Vaastu Shastra shapes the space; Jyotisha chooses the moment. Dr. Ravi Rao brings the two together, advising on the auspicious Muhurta for the key stages of a temple project.</p></div><ol class="temple-vaastu__timeline"><li><b>01</b><span>Consecration of the land<small>Bhoomi Pujan</small></span></li><li><b>02</b><span>Groundbreaking &amp; foundation<small>Shanku Sthapana</small></span></li><li><b>03</b><span>Start of construction</span></li><li><b>04</b><span>Murti installation<small>Murti Sthapana</small></span></li><li><b>05</b><span>Consecration of the deity<small>Prana Pratishtha</small></span></li></ol><p class="temple-vaastu__timeline-link"><a class="temple-vaastu__link" href="<?php echo esc_url($rr_tv_muhurta_url); ?>">Explore the Muhurta Calendar &nbsp;→</a></p></div></section>
<section class="temple-vaastu__section temple-vaastu__section--rituals" id="rituals"><div class="temple-vaastu__container"><div class="temple-vaastu__rituals-intro"><div><p class="temple-vaastu__eyebrow temple-vaastu__eyebrow--light">05 / Temple consecration &amp; sacred rituals</p><h2 class="temple-vaastu__title">From sacred architecture to divine presence</h2><div class="temple-vaastu__ornament temple-vaastu__ornament--left"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 30" width="260" height="30" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="#ffd479" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M0 15H96M164 15H260" stroke-opacity=".75"/><path d="M130 3C139 9 141 19 130 27C119 19 121 9 130 3Z"/><path d="M130 27C122 26 113 21 109 11C118 11 126 17 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C138 26 147 21 151 11C142 11 134 17 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C119 28 107 25 100 18C111 15 123 19 130 27Z"/><path d="M130 27C141 28 153 25 160 18C149 15 137 19 130 27Z"/></g><circle cx="90" cy="15" r="2.4" fill="#fff1c9"/><circle cx="170" cy="15" r="2.4" fill="#fff1c9"/><circle cx="130" cy="15" r="2.6" fill="#fff1c9"/></svg></div><p class="temple-vaastu__text">The establishment of a Hindu temple is a sacred journey that extends beyond architectural planning and construction. From the first rituals performed on the land to the consecration of the deity, each stage carries profound spiritual significance.</p><p class="temple-vaastu__text">Dr. Ravi Rao provides personalized guidance and conducts the sacred temple rituals together with his team of Brahmin priests, in accordance with the religious traditions and shastric requirements of each temple.</p></div><div class="temple-vaastu__rituals-photo" role="img" aria-label="Dr. Ravi Rao in prayer beside a brick fire pit prepared for a yajna"><span>RITUALS &nbsp;/&nbsp; CONSECRATION</span></div></div><div class="temple-vaastu__trishula"><div class="temple-vaastu__trishula-view" role="img" aria-label="A golden trishula with a damaru and a garland of hibi