<p class="temple-vaastu__text">With over 35 years of professional experience in Vaastu Shastra and Jyotisha, Dr. Ravi Rao brings together sacred architecture, auspicious timing and ritual practice in a single, coordinated approach to temple projects.</p>
<p class="temple-vaastu__text">His approach respects the sacred purpose of each temple, its presiding deity, established religious traditions and architectural requirements.</p>
<div class="temple-vaastu__step"><b>01</b><div><strong>Understanding the Temple Tradition</strong><span>Study of the purpose of the temple, its presiding deity, religious tradition and the specifics of the project.</span></div></div>
<div class="temple-vaastu__step"><b>02</b><div><strong>Sacred Land &amp; Vaastu Assessment</strong><span>Analysis of the land, orientation, spatial organization and sacred geometry.</span></div></div>
<div class="temple-vaastu__step"><b>03</b><div><strong>Temple Planning &amp; Expert Guidance</strong><span>Personalized recommendations and coordination with architects, sthapatis and temple committees.</span></div></div>
<div class="temple-vaastu__step"><b>04</b><div><strong>Muhurta &amp; Ritual Preparation</strong><span>Selection of auspicious timing and preparation for the sacred ceremonies.</span></div></div>
<div class="temple-vaastu__step"><b>05</b><div><strong>Sacred Rituals &amp; Consecration</strong><span>Conduct of the temple rituals together with his team of Brahmin priests.</span></div></div>
<div class="temple-vaastu__author"><span>35+ Years of Professional Practice · Founder of Astro-Vaastu Research Centre · Author on Vaastu Shastra &amp; Jyotisha</span></div>
