<details><summary>When should a Vaastu consultant be involved in temple construction?</summary><p>Ideally, Vaastu consultation should begin during site selection and the initial architectural planning stage, before construction commences.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can Vaastu consultations be provided for existing temples?</summary><p>Yes. Existing temples can be assessed to identify Vaastu defects and develop appropriate recommendations while respecting established religious traditions and architectural integrity.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can Vaastu recommendations be integrated into existing architectural plans?</summary><p>Yes. Existing architectural drawings and master plans can be reviewed, with recommendations developed in coordination with the project team.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can temple Vaastu consultation include ritual preparation and Muhurta selection?</summary><p>Yes. Dr. Ravi Rao combines Vaastu Shastra and Jyotisha to provide guidance on temple planning, auspicious timing, ritual preparation and consecration. You can also consult the <a class="temple-vaastu__link" href="<?php echo esc_url($rr_tv_muhurta_url); ?>">Muhurta Calendar</a>.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Dr. Ravi Rao conduct temple consecration ceremonies?</summary><p>Yes. Dr. Ravi Rao conducts sacred temple rituals, including Prana Pratishtha, together with his team of Brahmin priests.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can we request temple consecration services separately from Vaastu consultation?</summary><p>Yes. Sacred rituals and consecration ceremonies can also be arranged separately from a Vaastu consultation. To discuss your requirements, <a class="temple-vaastu__link" href="<?php echo esc_attr($rr_tv_contact); ?>">contact us</a> or visit <a class="temple-vaastu__link" href="https://www.navagrahamandalam.com/services-4118" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navagraha Mandalam</a>.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Dr. Ravi Rao work with temple trusts, architects and sthapatis?</summary><p>Yes. Consultations can involve temple trustees, architects, sthapatis and other professionals responsible for the planning and development of the temple.</p></details>
<details><summary>What information is required for a temple Vaastu consultation?</summary><p>Available site plans, architectural drawings, location details, information about the presiding deity and the temple tradition, together with the proposed scope of the project, provide a foundation for the initial assessment.</p></details></div></section>
